  "pre_freeze_revisions": {
    "what": "The protocol was written, read through once in full, and revised before this freeze. The revisions were wording, consistency and rigor fixes found on that read; none was prompted by any model result, because none exists.",
    "changes": [
      "reconciled the rule that a missing result is never filled with a pooled value with the C2 and C3 small-cell fallback (the fallback is part of the predictor's definition, counted and logged)",
      "target-level INSUFFICIENT_DATA now says counts, the base rate and its Wilson interval are still reported: what is insufficient is modelling",
      "fold-level INSUFFICIENT_DATA applies to every predictor, comparators included, so predictors are always compared on the same events",
      "the regression threshold states whether it applies to training, to the pooled development test set or to the holdout, and that the holdout result is COUNTS_ONLY",
      "bootstrap replicates raised from 2000 to 5000 so that a 99% tail is placed on more than ten resamples",
      "added a calibration policy: no Platt or isotonic transform is fitted in Milestone 4; calibration is assessed, not applied",
      "stated that terciles replace the contract's deciles; added 'same CIK' to the issuer-history definition; fixed the comparator wording in the acceptance text; added the integrity block"
    ]
  },
